# fca.py audit

- [ ] Does the formal context preserve exact object/attribute incidence?
- [ ] Are objects and attributes canonically ordered before hashing?
- [ ] Does Next Closure equal the independent brute-force oracle on every POC fixture?
- [ ] Are empty extents and the full-attribute closure handled according to FCA definitions?
- [ ] Is FCA used only for attribute closure, never as a substitute for temporal/causal edges?
- [ ] Are large-context brute-force calls rejected rather than allowed to explode silently?

